# Minimal UI Copy

KameOps UI should stay **clean and sparse**. Agents must not add explanatory text unless the user explicitly asks for copy.

## Default: no new text

- Do **not** add page descriptions, helper paragraphs, tooltips, subtitles, or `CardDescription` blocks unless the user requests them.
- Do **not** explain how a feature works in the UI (OAuth scopes, legacy paths, env vars, etc.) — that belongs in docs or settings reference, not on every screen.
- Do **not** duplicate the same message in title + description + body (e.g. login shell + form paragraph + button).
- Prefer **labels, buttons, badges, and data** over prose.

## When text is allowed

| Situation | OK to add text |
| --------- | ---------------- |
| User asks for copy, onboarding, or empty-state message | Yes — match their tone and length |
| Error / validation / toast | Short, actionable only |
| Empty state | One short line + CTA (unless user says otherwise) |
| Destructive confirm dialog | One clear question |
| Accessibility (`aria-label`, `sr-only`) | As needed — not visible clutter |

## Length limits (when text is required)

- **Page subtitle / description**: ≤ 1 short line (≤ 12 words) or omit
- **Card description**: omit by default; max 1 line if essential
- **Helper text under inputs**: only for non-obvious format (e.g. chat ID format)
- **Empty state**: title + one line + button — no bullet essays

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — unsolicited explanation
<AuthPageShell
  title="Sign in with Google"
  description="Grant Gmail and Calendar access so KameOps can automate your credit card SOA workflow"
>
  <p>KameOps uses your Google account to fetch statement PDFs…</p>
  <Button>Continue with Google</Button>
</AuthPageShell>

// ✅ GOOD — action speaks for itself
<AuthPageShell title="Sign in">
  <Button>Continue with Google</Button>
</AuthPageShell>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — CardDescription restates the title
<CardTitle>Gmail</CardTitle>
<CardDescription>
  Required for SOA PDF fetch from Gmail and optional due-date calendar events.
  Sign in with Google to grant gmail.readonly and calendar.events scopes.
</CardDescription>

// ✅ GOOD — status + action only
<CardTitle>Gmail</CardTitle>
<StatusBadge label="Connected" />
<Button>Reconnect</Button>
```

## Do not

- Add "marketing" or feature-list paragraphs to dashboard pages
- Paste env var names or file paths into UI (`configs/token.json`, `GOOGLE_CALENDAR_AUTO=1`)
- Add "Learn more" blocks without user request
- Expand copy "to be helpful" — ask the user if unsure
